| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=\\frac{3}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548046 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b82a91db-40b3-51bf-b539-d94cf7913732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548046 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}]-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548070 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548070 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146207" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548070 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548070 #edb/ref 1071 "| $y$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=3.3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548070 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e707f526-b15a-5f98-b415-f7cf137b340a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548070 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.35+(4)^{2}\\cdot 0.65]-{(3.3)}^{2} \\\\  & =1.4+10.4-10.89 \\\\  & =0.91.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548162 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548162 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c8a3756c-04e8-556f-9cc2-eccde7fa83d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548162 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186548070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548163 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548163 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c91da45b-8d0d-5c23-88c6-ad0898a0b0e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548163 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548167 #edb/ref